For the independent treatment and outcome roles of \(\mathrm{def:roles}\), define the nested outcome-role projection by
\[
 \widehat\eta_J^L(x)=\frac1\ell\sum_{j\in I_L}
       w_h(X_j)K_J(x,X_j)Y_j\qquad(x\in C_h),
 \qquad \widehat\eta_J^L(x)=0\qquad(x\notin C_h).
\]
As in \(\mathrm{def:projection}\), weighted basis expressions are zero outside \(C_h\). Define
\[
\begin{aligned}
 \widehat R_{h,J}
 &=\frac1\ell\sum_{j\in I_L}w_h(X_j)r(X_j)A_jY_j
   -\frac1t\sum_{i\in I_T}w_h(X_i^T)r(X_i^T)A_i^T
                     \widehat\eta_J^L(X_i^T)\\
 &=\frac1\ell\sum_{j\in I_L}w_h(X_j)r(X_j)A_jY_j
   -\frac1{t\ell}\sum_{i\in I_T}\sum_{j\in I_L}
       w_h(X_i^T)w_h(X_j)r(X_i^T)A_i^T
                    K_J(X_i^T,X_j)Y_j.
\end{aligned}
\]
The terminal response factor in the correction is \(Y_j\), not \(A_jY_j\). The first, uncorrected summand retains \(A_jY_j\). Define the matrices by the unchanged formulas
\[
\begin{aligned}
 \widehat Q^{\mathrm{raw}}_{h,J}
 &=\frac1\ell\sum_{j\in I_L}w_h(X_j)r(X_j)r(X_j)^\top A_j\\
 &\quad-\frac1{t\ell}\sum_{i\in I_T}\sum_{j\in I_L}
 w_h(X_i^T)w_h(X_j)r(X_i^T)r(X_j)^\top
 A_i^TA_jK_J(X_i^T,X_j),\\
 \widehat Q_{h,J}
 &=\frac{\widehat Q^{\mathrm{raw}}_{h,J}
        +(\widehat Q^{\mathrm{raw}}_{h,J})^\top}{2}.
\end{aligned}
\]
Every input is observed in \(\mathcal D_{n,m}\) under the role split in \(\mathrm{def:roles}\), including \(m=0\); outcomes from the treatment role are discarded. The nested display and the rectangular double sum define exactly the same vector.
